target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: a message nobody can print
why:    accumulating every row's error is right, but unbounded it turned a store with 10,000 bad rows for one run into a 1.3 MB error — measured — on a channel whose whole purpose is to be read by a person. Anchored with the comment below it because `if r.errN > maxRunErrs {` alone now matches twice: the finalise pass that reports the total carries the same condition one indent deeper, and an ambiguous anchor scores stale rather than mutating anything.
--- old
	if r.errN > maxRunErrs {
		// Bounded, because accumulating without a cap turned a store with 10,000 bad rows
--- new
	if false {
		// Bounded, because accumulating without a cap turned a store with 10,000 bad rows
